      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the equation of the line passing through the points \\((2, 2, 1)\\) and \\((5, 1, -2)\\). The general formula for the parametric equations of a line is derived as follows:\n\n1. The difference in coordinates:\n   - Displacement in the \\(x\\)-direction: \\(x = 2 + 3t\\)\n   - Displacement in the \\(y\\)-direction: \\(y = 1 - t\\)\n   - Displacement in the \\(z\\)-direction: \\(z = 1 - 3t\\)\n\nHere, \\(t\\) represents a parameter.\n\n2. The point \\(P\\) satisfies these parametric equations.\n   \n3. We are given that the \\(x\\)-coordinate of point \\(P\\) is 4. This gives us an equation to solve for \\(t\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 4 \\implies 4 = 2 + 3t\n   \\]\n\n4. Solving the equation for \\(t\\):\n   \\[\n   4 = 2 + 3t \\implies 3t = 2 \\implies t = \\frac{2}{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. Substituting \\(t = \\frac{2}{3}\\) into our equation \\(z = 1 - 3t\\):\n   \\[\n   z = 1 - 3 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = 1 - 2 = -1\n   \\]\n\nThus, the \\(z\\)-coordinate of the point is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
